  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Hawks and doves across the ice",
  "description": "Mark a lane across the ice with cones, about a third of the rink length wide, so nobody can escape too far. All the doves stand by one board with their stick in their hand. One or two hawks start in the middle.\n\nOn the coach's signal the doves skate across to the other board. Anyone caught by a hawk becomes a hawk for the next crossing. Keep going back and forth until only one or two doves are left – they start as hawks in the next round.\n\nVariant: each dove skates with a ball. A hawk catches a dove by winning or poking the ball away. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Low skating position and short, quick strides at the start."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Head up – see both the hawks and the other doves so nobody collides."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Change direction with strong strides when a hawk comes, not by stopping."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Stick in one hand with the blade down on the ice the whole time."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "phase": "warmup",
  "difficulty": 1,
